  "The gas flow the tank takes is a scenario switch (2, 4 or 6 mm/s). The input of that name is also the reference speed of Humbird's oxygen figure, so moving it alone rescales that figure ($48.56 to $48.68 in the low-lactate example) without changing any tank; it is left out.",
  "Maturation, the hours the cells spend in the tank without growing before harvest, is a choice of product, not an estimate. The products near market are bulk cell mass and take none; 4 to 28 days to mature muscle or fat would take the low-lactate example from $48.68 to $75.46 (4 days) or $232.75 (28 days). It is a lever on the page; it is left out here."
